{"agent":"lane2-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The queue command for a question ask is not a command an operator can run. For ask Q9, `collect_asks` now sets `command` to `ddflow approvals answer Q9 --text <answer>` (and `ddflow approvals answer 'weird id' --text <answer>` when the id needs quoting). In a shell, an unquoted `<answer>` is stdin redirection from a file named `answer`, not a placeholder, so pasting the suggested line fails with a missing file or never passes `--text`. Approve rows stay a real verb (`ddflow approvals approve {rid}`); question rows, the case this bug was opened for, are not. `tests/test_digest_queue.py` locks the broken string in, so the regression never catches it. Quote the placeholder (`--text '<answer>'`) or omit `--text` until a real answer exists.","digest":"859a05cd3a5c121b","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/digest/collect_asks.py:71","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/digest/collect_asks.py:71"}],"chunks_total":2,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":10691,"diff_sha":"cf766fe89907438cca895e4c0dfceae6810ed374c6b0d290ed72df7156ca8a78","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-ask-question-no-answer-verb","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":58.1,"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"150dae6acbb31b11","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-ask-question-no-answer-verb.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261110T224254Z-7bcd57f4.jsonl","reason":"","review_id":"2dce81b1c905","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"a5f11fdeaa893e32000c617ee452abe7d6ee84ef","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/approvals_answer.py":"100644 62494c39791ff1cfa391114ffc0df2344012bc05","ddflow/services/approvals/answer.py":"100644 b5f1316cc2d9